# The gcp-infra profile: the Google Cloud project every Cloud Run service shares, described in
# OpenTofu. Opt in with `gcp-infra` in the project's .template-profiles; it needs no other
# profile. Same syntax as .template/manifest, but every path is read from
# .template/profiles/gcp-infra/ rather than from the template's root.
#
# It manages the make targets (.devtools/gcp-infra.mk, which base.mk includes), the generator
# in .devtools/gcp-infra/ and the OpenTofu pin and hook. The `gcp` profile builds on it.
# What it makes in infra/: the state bucket's backend, the project's APIs (Cloud Run, Artifact
# Registry, Secret Manager, Pub/Sub, Vertex AI and Telemetry, Cloud Trace, Monitoring and
# Logging), the Artifact Registry repository, a runtime account per environment that can write
# traces and metrics, the budget, and Workload Identity Federation with the deployer and the
# builder accounts that deploy.yml signs in as.
#
# Per project, and not listed: everything under infra/, and the workflow that deploys.
# `make -C .devtools infra-gen` writes a first infra/, which reads DEPLOY_ENVS from
# .devtools/Makefile like the gcp profile does; with the gcp profile, `gen.mjs host` writes it.
#
# The mise.toml, lefthook.yml, .gitignore and .editorconfig blocks are named gcp, as they were
# when the gcp profile held them, so a project that has them is updated in place. The
# lefthook.yml block only points at .devtools/lefthook-gcp-infra.yml, which holds the hook.

file  .devtools/gcp-infra.mk
file  .devtools/gcp-infra/scaffold.mjs
file  .devtools/gcp-infra/gen.mjs

block mise.toml       gcp
file  .devtools/lefthook-gcp-infra.yml
block lefthook.yml    gcp
block .gitignore      gcp
block .editorconfig   gcp
block AGENTS.md       gcp-infra
